{
  "_comment": "Properties of a front-panel control or indicator that a Property Node bound to a control of the VI may write while the VI runs (plan section 10). A row is identified by its PropItemCode, never its stored name; a row of several path segments (Scale.Maximum, Caption.Text) by the codes of its segments joined with '.' (a one-segment row's key is its code alone). 'inherited' holds the codes every Control class shares; 'classes' holds the codes a class declares, once, on the class NI documents the property on (its 'doc_url' shows the class path), and every class below it in 'class_parents' finds it there (a class entry wins over an inherited one with the same code; a strict and a non-strict reference of a class are one class). A Property Node on a wired control reference reads and writes every listed property through the panel, the same property a bound Property Node reads and writes: a read before any write gives the value the file starts the control in (the decoded members, parser/fp_starting_properties.py), else the 'default', else it raises NotImplementedError naming the property. Each entry: 'name' is NI's long name, 'member' the Python name, 'value' the kind of value written, as the Python value the generated code passes (bool: bool; enum: the property's integer enum value; number: int or float; string: str; path: pathlib.Path; color: int, LabVIEW's 0x00RRGGBB color; string_array: list of str, a list of lists of str for a two-dimensional array; number_array: list of int or float; array: list of the elements the wire carries, a cluster staying a cluster; cluster: the cluster the wire carries), 'doc_url' NI's public page for the property. 'value_codes' lists the codes of the property that reads or writes a control's value (the Value row), by the same inherited-then-class rule. 'value_signaling_codes' lists, by the same rule, the codes of Value (Signaling), which writes the value and generates a Value Change event (NI: write only). A property is listed only when NI's page says what it does. 'reference_rows' lists the rows a Property Node on a wired control reference (a Ctl, Clust, Bool ... reference) reads or writes as the reference's own value, indicator flag or label text, or a cluster's Controls[], or an array's Array Element (NI: 'Reference to the array element', read only): each row's 'codes' are the property paths (one code per segment) the corpus records for it; 'value' adds the generic Value code to 'value_codes' (a strict class's own code, 104013842, is already there). Code 104013825 is the Disabled property as a Property Node saved in LabVIEW 8.2 stores it (an integer, the enum written as its number); the file's own enum constants wired to it list enabled 0, disabled 1, greyed out 2, the values of DisabledEnum (NI forum, \"Possible Issue with help for disable property node\": the 8.2 property is the U8 form of the 9.0 enum, same values), so it shares that entry's page and member.",
  "class_parents": {
    "_comment": "The VI Server class each class of 'classes' belongs to, from NI's class hierarchy (https://docs-be.ni.com/api/bundle/labview-api-ref/page/properties-and-methods/vi-server/class-hierarchy.html): a class finds a property on its own entry, then on its parent's, up to Control, whose properties are 'inherited'. A class with no entry here is a class of Control. GObject and Decoration sit above Control, so a Decoration (Decor) has none of Control's properties (Visible is NI's page under gobject/control). NamedNumeric holds Ring's and Enum's shared Strings[]; GraphChart the properties of a Waveform Chart, a Waveform Graph (and its XY Graph) and an Intensity Graph; a Combo Box is a String.",
