  "generic_classes": {
    "_comment": "The classes of a Property Node whose reference can be any object of a front panel or a block diagram: Generic (heap name Gen), the class every VI Server class descends from, and GObject (GObj), the class of every front-panel and block-diagram object (NI's class hierarchy, https://docs-be.ni.com/api/bundle/labview-api-ref/page/properties-and-methods/vi-server/class-hierarchy.html). Which kind the reference is, is told by what made it (codegen/nodes/reference_origin.py).",
    "classes": ["Generic", "Gen", "GObject", "GObj"]
  },
  "block_diagram_roots": {
    "_comment": "The classes of NI's class hierarchy (https://docs-be.ni.com/api/bundle/labview-api-ref/page/properties-and-methods/vi-server/class-hierarchy.html) that sit directly under GObject and are objects of a block diagram: AbstractDiagram (and its Diagram), Terminal, Constant, Tunnel, SequenceLocal, Node (and its SubVI, Structure, ...), Wire, PropertyItem, FlatSequence and its two tunnels, PolymorphicVISelector. A reference whose class is one of them or below one (class_parents) is a reference to a block-diagram object, which converted code does not have. Pnl, Pane, Decoration, Scale and Control, the other classes under GObject, are front-panel objects. The short names (Diag, Term, SubVI, CaseSel, ...) are the heap class names the Property Node records, each the abbreviation of the NI class listed as its parent.",
